  "name": "Question 5",
  "problem": "The cubic polynomial $f(x)$ has roots ${x}_{1}=6,\\,{x}_{2,3}=\\pm 3\\text{i},$ and the coefficient of the cubic term is $-4.$ Find $f(x).$\n\n$f(x)=$\n{{field-1}}${x}^{3}\\,+$\n{{field-2}}${x}^{2}\\,-$\n{{field-3}}$x\\,+$\n{{field-4}}",
  "worked_solution": "Since $f(x)$ has roots ${x}_{1}=6$ and ${x}_{2,3}=\\pm 3\\text{i},$ and the coefficient of the cubic term is $a=-4,$ we can write the polynomial as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =a(x-{x}_{1})(x-{x}_{2})(x-{x}_{3}) \\\\  & =-4(x-6)(x-3\\text{i})(x-(-3\\text{i})) \\\\  & =-4(x-6)(x-3\\text{i})(x+3\\text{i})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpanding the parentheses, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-4(x-6)(x-3\\text{i})(x+3\\text{i}) & = \\\\ -4(x-6)({x}^{2}-x(-3\\text{i})-x(3\\text{i})+(3\\text{i})(-3\\text{i})) & = \\\\ -4(x-6)({x}^{2}+9) & = \\\\ -4({x}^{3}-6{x}^{2}+9x-54) & = \\\\ -4{x}^{3}+24{x}^{2}-36x+216.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $f(x)=-4{x}^{3}+24{x}^{2}-36x+216.$",
